Issues.Body:
### .NET version

11.0.0, 10.0.12

### Did it work in .NET Framework?

Yes

### Did it work in any of the earlier releases of .NET Core or .NET 5+?

Not tested/verified

### Issue description

The customer's application encounters System.IndexOutOfRangeException while loading a form that contains a CheckedListBox. After the list's items, selection, and checked states have been set, enabling the horizontal scrollbar in the form's Load handler triggers the exception and interrupts the affected control's initialization. The customer reports that the issue occurs with some item counts and checked states but not others.

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4ff14798-f5aa-406b-9311-7947c5e0328d

### Steps to reproduce

1. Open the desired project in Visual Studio, build it, and start debugging.
2. During initialization in the constructor, before the control's native handle is created, it adds "A", sets SelectedIndex=0, and reads SelectedItems.Count.
3. It adds "B" and then sets HorizontalScrollbar=true.
4. Observe System.IndexOutOfRangeException at the HorizontalScrollbar assignment in the form's constructor, before the form is displayed.

The reproduction code in the form's constructor is:

```
public ReproForm()
{
    CheckedListBox list = new CheckedListBox { Dock = DockStyle.Fill };
    Controls.Add(list);

    list.Items.Add("A");
    list.SelectedIndex = 0;
    _ = list.SelectedItems.Count;
    list.Items.Add("B");
    list.HorizontalScrollbar = true;
}
```
